# diclofenac.msf
# Diclofenac  pKa=4.150 (COOH→COO-, q=0→-1)
# Source: Manallack 2007 / NIST
# NSAID COX-2 inhibitor. ArCH2COOH with 2,6-diCl phenyl and NH bridge.
# The NH is non-ionisable (amide-like resonance with NO2-analog geometry);
# only the carboxylate ionises in the physiological range.
# Clinical relevance: pKa=4.15 → extensively ionised at intestinal pH.

